{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/353735-changeling-the-lost-hacks-for-higher-power-level","id":353735,"title":"Changeling the Lost: Hacks for higher power level","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-29T08:07:12-08:00","id":353735,"title":"Changeling the Lost: Hacks for higher power level","content":"Are there any hacks out there worth looking for changeling the lost? Anything from Mirrors maybe?<br /> <br /> Like if I wanted to make Changeling closer in power level/abilities to the fae in the comic book series Fables for example, any recommended hacks or just make the characters with more experience points?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2127-eltacolibre","name":"Eltacolibre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2127_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-29T15:48:33-08:00","id":354138,"title":"","content":"Well, there are a couple of ways you could do it:<br /> <br /> 1) Your changeling has Wyrd 6 or more, and thus can sign and invoke custom clauses of Contracts that are also rated at 6 or more. This can give you versions of already present clauses that have greater duration/reach/potence/finesse, or wholly new effects. You could, for example, have Stone 6, which could allow you to attack the ground with your fists or feet and create structures out of rock and concrete and other hard materials in a radius around you proportional to your sucesses. At Wyrd 10, you could have 10 dot clauses, which can and should be genuinely epic.<br /> <br /> 2) Modify the Token Maker Merit (Rites Of Spring - From The Thorns Chapter) so that you can not only craft Tokens faster, but you can also craft Tokens rated at 6 dots or more. This can be limited by your Wyrd like option number 1, at you discretion.<br /> <br /> 3) Give changelings of Wyrd 6 or more the ability to buy a Merit that lets them incorporate Epic Aspects into Pledges. Epic Aspects can include the 8 Again bonus, up to your Wyrd in bonus dice to most rolls, rote quality, advanced action and give/enhance supernatural powers at your discretion.<br /> <br /> 4) Give changelings of Wyrd 6 or more the ability to buy a Merit that allows them to invest 10 or even 15 dots into Hedgespun Items and give them unusual qualities, such as blades that deal aggravated to certain beings at the cost of glamour/willpower/health points. Be mindful of what limits you want, however: I would rule that any Hedgespun Item cannot give a dice bonus that is 5 dice greater than its normal counterpart. So, if Hedgespun weapons in your game start with a dice bonus equal to their normal versions, you can make a sword (+3L) out of Hedgespun that has +8L by investing 5 dots into it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 12-29-2014, 07:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-29T18:13:55-08:00","id":354213,"title":"","content":"That sounds pretty good actually, I'll work on starting characters with wyrd 6 and the proposed customization sounds like what I want out of a fable-like game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2127-eltacolibre","name":"Eltacolibre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2127_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-29T18:26:17-08:00","id":354224,"title":"","content":"No problem. Also, if youre feeling especially heroic or power hungry, you can challenge True Fae to Feuds and gain their Titles if you win. Titles can include powerful objects, small armies of servant creatures, a single but powerful avatar and entire locations. For more information on Feuds and Titles, consult The Equinox Road, chapters three and five.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-29T18:44:05-08:00","id":354245,"title":"","content":"Yeah I'll get on reading Equinox Road, I remember reading it back in the day, but since I never got to these high levels changeling, didn't remember most of it. Titles would be something great to push the players for some adventures. Now, to decide how much xp to give.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2127-eltacolibre","name":"Eltacolibre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2127_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-29T19:00:19-08:00","id":354261,"title":"","content":"How much higher-powered is <i>Fables</i>? I've never read it, so help me out a bit in understanding what you're shooting for. Changelings can already be pretty powerful when they stack the deck, buuuut... like everyone else so far, they're almost certainly going to receive a power buff in the game's second edition. Some of this is simply from experience, rather than an outright &quot;They must be X much stronger than before!&quot; Better power design, more options, and new ways of interacting with the vastly improved WoD 2E base system will help really make them stronger, I think.<br /> <br /> Of course, that doesn't much help you <i>now</i>, but hopefully you'll be eagerly anticipating a second edition!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-29T19:14:43-08:00","id":354286,"title":"","content":"Well the big thing about the fables in general, they basically gain powers depending on how popular they are with the mundies (normal people) but something that is common of most fables:<br /> <br /> -Immortality: Basically dying of old age is unheard of.<br /> <br /> -Hard to Kill and Powers: Somewhat, a fable can take multiple fatal wounds and survive, like bullets to the head or even an axe to the head, they have accelerated healing, basically in general they are very tough to kill. Other powers vary, like bigby, the big bad wolf is of course very strong and can take a Large wolf form and has the ability to blow brick houses with just the power of his breath inherited from his father the North wind (long story). Combat heavy, fables have of course super strength and other similar abilities. Dragons and Giants are ridiculously powerful, but most of the time, they are kept asleep to avoid troubles. Powers vary from spells, curses, elemental control, magic items of legend etc...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2127,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2127-eltacolibre","user":"Eltacolibre","date":". 12-29-2014, 10:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2127-eltacolibre","name":"Eltacolibre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2127_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}